-- title:
--   Origin chart modulo ((X/Y)^q,(Z/Y)^q) is T[u]/(u^q)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a natural number, $T$ a commutative ring and $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$, with associated projective model `W.toProjective`. Let $S$ denote the graded quotient $T[X_0,X_1,X_2]/(F)$ by the ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic $F$ of `W.toProjective`, graded by the images of the homogeneous submodules, and let $\mathcal O =$ `OriginChartRing W.toProjective` be the degree-zero part of the homogeneous localisation of $S$ away from the class $Y$ of $X_1$; inside it, `xOverY` and `zOverY` are the degree-zero fractions $X/Y$ and $Z/Y$ given by the classes of $X_0$ and $X_2$ over $Y$. The assertion is that there exists a ring isomorphism $e$ from $\mathcal O/(\,(X/Y)^q,\ (Z/Y)^q\,)$ onto $\mathrm{AdjoinRoot}(X^q) = T[X]/(X^q)$ such that, first, for every $t \in T$ the image under $e$ of the class of the degree-zero scalar coming from $t$ (the image of $t$ under $T \to S_0 \to \mathcal O$) is the image of $t$ under the structure map $T \to T[X]/(X^q)$, and second, $e$ sends the class of $X/Y$ to the root class of $X$ in $T[X]/(X^q)$. No smoothness or characteristic hypothesis is imposed, and $q = 0$ is allowed, in which case both rings are zero. The isomorphism is asserted to exist, not to be unique, and its value on the class of $Z/Y$ is not recorded.
--
--   This is the algebraic identification of the $q$-th order neighbourhood of the origin section in the origin chart $D_+(Y)$ of a Weierstrass model: modulo $((X/Y)^q,(Z/Y)^q)$ the chart cubic solves $Z/Y$ as a power series in the nilpotent parameter $X/Y$, so the quotient is the truncated polynomial ring $T[u]/(u^q)$ with $u$ the class of $X/Y$. It feeds the finiteness, flatness and rank computation [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.isFinite_pullback_snd_kwZeroSect_flat_finrank_eq_of_zChart_pow_originChart_pow`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.isFinite_pullback_snd_kwZeroSect_flat_finrank_eq_of_zChart_pow_originChart_pow).
